                        "form": "стяжа́телях"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "968864a4-7126-305b-8777-12c8d6ad3bd1",
                        "entry_id": "d0e8eb48-60cd-352d-8979-ea76ae299700",
                        "glosses": [
                            "устар. тот, кто стяжает, добивается чего-либо"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f4ab121c-a76e-4d01-a6e5-94f8c449045e",
                                "sense_id": "968864a4-7126-305b-8777-12c8d6ad3bd1",
                                "text": "В городе я бываю в центре умственных течений, искусства, литературы, вижу счастливых спортсменов, любовников, всякого рода стяжателей героических замыслов и действий."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2f235c0c-07b1-33cf-94a0-6db538aa08dc",
                        "entry_id": "d0e8eb48-60cd-352d-8979-ea76ae299700",
                        "glosses": [
                            "книжн. человек, стремящийся к наживе, накоплению денег, материальных богатств, занимающийся стяжанием, стяжательством"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f9c98529-2dc5-4d90-9327-ff01dafe9f15",
                                "sense_id": "2f235c0c-07b1-33cf-94a0-6db538aa08dc",
                                "text": "Стяжатель по натуре, Кишкин тащил в свою каморку решительно всё, что мог достать тем или другим путём, — старую газету, которую выпрашивал почитать у кого-нибудь из компанейских служащих, железный крюк, найденный на дороге, образцы разных горных пород и т. д."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "858b46d7-968e-43b6-b65d-397ec0847dd9",
                                "sense_id": "2f235c0c-07b1-33cf-94a0-6db538aa08dc",
                                "text": "Все они сперва великие грешники, потом великие враги греха, сперва великие стяжатели, потом великие расточители."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7862ac66-262c-4a91-80aa-35ea4560de3f",
                        "source_entry_id": "d0e8eb48-60cd-352d-8979-ea76ae299700",
                        "target_lang_word": "grubber",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "grubber",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "91f3dcfd-968f-3077-9b75-d59edd3437ba",
                                        "entry_id": "83414bd5-851f-343c-b8ef-e007c6bd3b91",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who grubs."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2eeafb6e-1fd2-332b-b803-1e5270076919",
                                        "entry_id": "83414bd5-851f-343c-b8ef-e007c6bd3b91",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A tool, implement, or machine of the nature of a grub axe, grub hook, etc; (dialectal) a cultivator."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ad855a16-462f-3e7c-88f3-921413f2504f",
                                        "entry_id": "83414bd5-851f-343c-b8ef-e007c6bd3b91",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An attacking short-distance kick in behind the defence in which the ball is bounced along the ground, using the uneven bounce of the ball to make it difficult for the defence to retrieve."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b6c52d8e-d52d-4f00-a474-9321f6ccd395",
                                                "sense_id": "ad855a16-462f-3e7c-88f3-921413f2504f",
                                                "text": "England had an early opportunity with a line-out deep in French territory after a clever grubber from Foden only for Lionel Nallet to burgle back possession, and they then tore into France again as Alexis Palisson was smashed backwards after taking a garryowen and Manu Tuilagi thundered into Morgan Parra."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0ed83222-3092-4d34-acdf-88fb33d7ed54",
                                                "sense_id": "ad855a16-462f-3e7c-88f3-921413f2504f",
                                                "text": "Take that brilliant backline move off a scrum when Kolbe came off his left wing to put in a neat grubber for Arendse on the right wing to almost round the defense in the corner."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "67fc2151-f703-3fc8-8dfd-e0d947036d3c",
                                        "entry_id": "83414bd5-851f-343c-b8ef-e007c6bd3b91",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A ball that bounces unusually low such that it is difficult for the batsman to hit properly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a554fe72-d75c-3dfa-8942-1226f4378333",
                                        "entry_id": "83414bd5-851f-343c-b8ef-e007c6bd3b91",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A sweetshop."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "dated",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4d87c17d-9ddc-41a8-83d1-1b55bfdf3d5f",
                                                "sense_id": "a554fe72-d75c-3dfa-8942-1226f4378333",
                                                "text": "He could, moreover, no longer be tempted to the Grubber, for all chocolate and sweets were taboo."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "34129eef-f2df-401c-9159-f795a8b28d17",
                                                "sense_id": "a554fe72-d75c-3dfa-8942-1226f4378333",
                                                "text": "I remember the grubber which smelt of potato chips and chocolate and the steam-heated library with books about monasteries that no one else seemed to look at, and I remember the fresh weedless lawns between the school buildings […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "10e55384-1700-40a2-a5a5-fba69ab4a516",
                        "source_entry_id": "d0e8eb48-60cd-352d-8979-ea76ae299700",
                        "target_lang_word": "turnpenny",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "40c5d351-3c9a-4d95-8834-75cf7f84a2a0",
                        "source_entry_id": "d0e8eb48-60cd-352d-8979-ea76ae299700",
